{
  "title": "Myositis Ossificans",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pathology/8042/myositis-ossificans",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Oct 27 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Myositis Ossificans is a reactive soft tissue bone-forming process that commonly occurs following a traumatic event to soft tissues.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The condition typically presents in patients between ages 15 and 35 who develop pain, tenderness, swelling, and decreased range of motion following localized trauma.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with radiographs showing peripheral bone formation with central lucent area within soft tissues.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually observation as lesions typically resolve over time. Surgical excision is indicated for lesions that remain persistently symptomatic.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most common in young active males (15 to 35 years old)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic locations",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "quadriceps, brachialis and gluteal muscles",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A form of heterotopic ossification that is the result of",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**direct trauma**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**intramuscular hematoma**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "most common location is the diaphysis of long bones",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Must differentiate from tumors",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Fibrodysplasia ossificans progressiva (FOP) is a rare subtype of heterotopic ossification",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "involves mutation of the **ACVR1** gene (activin A type I receptor gene, a BMP type-1 receptor)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Genetics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "almost always a posttraumatic condition",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain, tenderness, swelling and decreased range of motion that usually presents within days of the injury",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "pain and size of the mass decrease with time",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "mass increases in size over several months (usually 3 to 6 cm)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "after the mass stops growing, it becomes firm",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "palpable soft tissue mass",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "restricted range of motion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Laboratory testing",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Initial elevation of the inflammatory cascade (CRP, CPK)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Mature phase elevation of serum alkaline phosphatase",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "peripheral bone formation with central lucent area",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may appear as \"dotted veil\" pattern",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI with gadolinium",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "rim enhancement is seen within the first 3 weeks",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT scan",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "lesion has an eggshell appearance",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Histology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Characteristic histology shows zonal pattern",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**periphery of lesion**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "mature trabeculae of lamellar and woven bone",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "calcification seen on xray",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**center of the lesion**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "irregular mass of immature fibroblasts",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "cartilage component may be present",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "(no calcification seen on xray)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "no cellular atypia seen",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "rest, range of motion exercises, and activity modification",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "passive stretching is contraindicated (makes it worse)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "physical therapy",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "utilized to maintain range of motion",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "radiographic monitoring",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "obtained to confirm maturation of the lesion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "surgical excision",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indicated only if it remains a problem after it matures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**do not operate in acute phase, wait at least six months**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**excision of the lesion within 6 to 12 months predisposes to local recurrence**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Usually self limiting",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "mass usually begins to decrease in size after 1 year",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
